=== REASONING ===
Direct API URL construction belonged at the shared client boundary. Target modules should call request() with prefixless API paths, and browser-owned URL flows should use the shared apiUrl() helper instead of spelling /api/v1 in feature code.
The API Playground request executor is retained as the explicit playground exception because it must expose raw status, headers, text bodies, and arbitrary user-entered request execution. Its OpenAPI discovery path uses request('/system/openapi') with text response parsing through the shared client.
The optional client.ts change is necessary to centralize apiUrl(), support text OpenAPI responses, and preserve watch API-key behavior without duplicating prefix handling. The optional useTelemetry.ts change is necessary so useVehicleLive can load initial live signals through a telemetry hook backed by request('/signals/{vehicleId}/live').
=== CHANGES ===
Replaced devtools, polling, settings, watch, and live-signal runtime fetches with request() or shared API client helpers using prefixless paths.
Moved target relative API imports to @/ aliases and removed the targeted /api/v1 comment drift.
Kept exactly one ApiPlaygroundPage fetch for user-entered request execution and migrated OpenAPI discovery to request().
